# fidelity TLS trust anchors -- the ONLY roots this suite trusts.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  A rented Vast host presented a certificate for
# huggingface.co with a hostname mismatch and UNEXPECTED_EOF
# (docs/CLOUD-RECIPES.md, 2026-09-05): the signature of a man-in-the-middle TLS
# proxy, on a box we were about to put an HF token on.  Python's default
# SSLContext reads the AMBIENT trust store and honours SSL_CERT_FILE /
# SSL_CERT_DIR, so where somebody else is root "verification passed" can mean
# "the store the host controls said yes".  fidelity.tlsguard verifies against
# THIS file and nothing else, so no environment variable and no on-box store
# can widen our trust.
#
# WHY ROOTS, NOT A LEAF PIN.  A leaf or intermediate pin breaks on every
# rotation, and a guard that hard-fails on a legitimate rotation gets routed
# around -- which is worse than the risk it prevents, because it also teaches
# people that the refusal is noise.  These are long-lived, self-signed roots
# (earliest expiry 2035): interception by a host-installed CA fails against
# them, while a Hub or provider certificate rotation inside these issuers does
# not.
#
# WHAT IS IN HERE, AND WHY.  Every root below is either MEASURED as
# terminating a chain this suite depends on, or the same operator's rotation
# sibling.  Each is self-signed (issuer == subject), and
# bin/selftest_tlsguard.py recomputes every digest from the bytes, refuses a
# root that is not self-signed, refuses one expiring within a year, and refuses
# any subject CN not in tlsguard.EXPECTED_ROOT_SUBJECT_CNS -- so adding a root
# is a deliberate two-file change, never an accident.
#
# ROTATION REMEDY.  If a peer we depend on moves to a CA that is not here, the
# refusal says so and names the fix: add the root, update
# tlsguard.BUNDLE_SHA256, re-run bin/selftest_tlsguard.py -- or unblock the run
# immediately under DISCLOSURE with FIDELITY_TLS_TRUST_BUNDLE=/path/to.pem,
# which is recorded in the attestation document and never silent.
#
# Do not regenerate this file by copying a system store: the ambient store is a
# moving target (this box's carries 121 certificates and no longer carries
# DigiCert Global Root CA at all).  Extract deliberately, cross-check each
# fingerprint against the CA operator's published value, and commit the review.

